msa2snp used first sequence as reference. It removes all gaps from first sequence in MSA to give the positions of variants.
--> Positions of variants refers to the positions in ungapped reference sequence

IGNORE THIS --> Script "CorrectPositions_GetMSA.Rmd" used for tasks mentioned below :

Our consensus will contain gaps (If visualized in NCBI MSA VIEWER the fisrt sequence is the consensus sequence generated according to input MSA) - To map positions of variants to MSA posiitons instead of first sequences (gaps-removed) I added in variant_position the number of gaps observed from start uptill that variant position. So now variant positions refer to positions in our consensus sequense generated by NCBI MSA VIEWER having gaps or MSA positions 
 - To extract unique copies only : MSA of there Variants was created using script in CorrectPositions_GetMSA.Rmd notebook for each chromosome and visualized in NCBI_Viewer
From these MSA, unique copies for each chromosome were identified and extracted from each MSA using python script "get_morphs_out.py" and stored in
file "unique_morphs_extracted_from_MSA_per_chr.aln". all the unique morphs in one chromosome were also uniques as compared to unique morphs in other chromosomes - variant positionsa mapped to T2T coordinates - SNPs/INDELS column added - Regions added (5'ETS, 18S , ITS1_repeat, 28S , ITS2, 5.8S, 3'ETS) - output file containinga all above data : variants_metadata.tsv


